# The packages hi's header checks for. Copy this file to
# ~/.config/say-hi/packages and edit it there - the copy in the tree is the
# default say-hi ships, and editing it dirties the checkout `hi --update` pulls into.
# `hi --packages-preview` renders what the priorities below do: each one's
# colors, a real example of each from this file, then the check itself.
#group,package:priority,package2:priority2...
# Every tier below reports a package that is missing as well as one that is
# present - that nudge is the point - and $_HI_PACKAGES_MIN_PRIORITY is the
# dial that decides how far down the list you want to hear about. It ships at
# 1, so tier 0 is off until you ask for it. Tier 4 is the one exception and the
# only thing that hides: see common/header.sh.
#
# 5: bright green installed, bright red missing - the tools whose absence
#    changes how you work
asdf:5
direnv:5
sshpass:5

# 4: hidden installed, yellow missing - the tools any working box has, hi's
#    own dependencies among them. A healthy target says nothing here; a bare
#    one says exactly what it is missing
