# 2: green installed, yellow missing - system and package tools
# One line per *question*, not per tool, wherever the answers are mutually
# exclusive: check_line renders the first name on the line that resolves, so
# grouping things no single machine has together collapses a column of `x`
# marks into one honest row. A Debian box has no business reporting that it is
# missing `choco`, `brew` and `apk`.
#
# Order inside a line is the tiebreak, because equal priorities are settled by
# file order: the native manager comes before the helper that wraps it (pacman
# before yay, dnf/zypper before rpm, brew before mas), so a machine that has
# both names shows the one that actually owns the packages.
apt-get:2,dnf:2,pacman:2,zypper:2,apk:2,brew:2,choco:2,chocolatey:2,yay:2,rpm:2,mas:2
# ...and the layers that sit *on top* of the native one. These can coexist -
# Ubuntu ships both snap and flatpak - so this is a "do you have any of these"
# row rather than an exclusive choice, which is still one row instead of four.
flatpak:2,snap:2,nix:2,appimage:2
sshfs:2
sshm:2
nano:2,micro:2,vim:2,pico:2,nvim:2,vi:2,emacs:2

